8.5  Writing the answer
A make-or-buy answer has five parts and the exam rewards each.
The comparison, as a column of differences, with the avoidable costs identified. Not two full costings.
The treatment of the unavoidable overhead, stated explicitly. One sentence — "the $315,000 of factory and head office overhead continues whichever is chosen and is excluded" — earns a mark and prevents the commonest error.
The opportunity cost of released capacity, if any, with its source named. If the question gives no alternative use, say that none has been identified and that the recommendation would change at a value of $105,000 a year or more.
The indifference price, as a negotiating position.
The qualitative factors that bear on this particular component, chosen rather than recited. For a lid that seals a food product, quality and dependability lead; for a cleaning contract they do not.
And the recommendation, which on the facts of section 8.1 is to go on making the lids, to ask the supplier for a price below 0.39, and to re-open the question if a use for the pressing shop is found.
YOUR TURN   Decide on a bracket
Figure F708-06 gives a component a company presently makes. Complete the blanks. Answers are at the end of the chapter.
Figure F708-06. Your turn: make or buy (complete the blanks)
@table
Item | Data | Answer
Variable cost of making a unit | Materials 1.40, labour 0.90, variable overhead 0.50 | ________
Annual variable cost | 400,000 units a year | ________
Avoidable fixed costs | A supervisor at 60,000 and machine insurance of 9,000 | ________
Total relevant cost of making | | ________
Cost of buying | Supplier price 3.20 a unit | ________
Better by | | ________
Indifference price | | ________
@end
LANGUAGE FOCUS   "Outsourcing"
English outsourcing means buying from outside what was previously made inside, and it carries overtones in ordinary use — of job losses, of distance, of something done cheaply — that the technical term does not. Offshoring is a different idea again: moving work to another country, which may be outsourced to a supplier or kept inside the company. Arabic الاستعانة بمصادر خارجية is literal and neutral, and the distinction from offshoring has to be made with النقل إلى الخارج. French externalisation is the settled term for outsourcing and délocalisation for offshoring, and French keeps the two apart more cleanly than English does. In an exam answer, use make or buy for the decision and outsourcing only where the question does.
