B is wrong. That omits the avoidable fixed costs.
C is wrong. That is full absorbed cost.
D is wrong. That is the avoidable fixed cost alone.
P8-04  Answer A. 3,500,000 × 0.42 = 1,470,000.
B is wrong. That is the cost of making.
C is wrong. That is the variable cost of making.
D is wrong. That is the difference.
P8-05  Answer A. It is a benefit obtainable only if the lids are bought.
B is wrong. It reduces the net cost.
C is wrong. It is the figure that can reverse the decision.
D is wrong. It belongs on the buying side.
P8-06  Answer A. 1,365,000 ÷ 3,500,000 = 0.39.
B is wrong. That is the supplier's quote.
C is wrong. That is the full absorbed cost.
D is wrong. That is the variable cost alone.
P8-07  Answer A. Delivery risk is a judgment.
B is wrong. That is a figure.
C is wrong. That is a figure.
D is wrong. That is a figure.
P8-08  Answer A. Fixed becomes variable, so the breakeven falls.
B is wrong. Fixed costs fall.
C is wrong. Leverage falls with them.
